        "thread_id": "TH4",
        "thread_goal": "Discuss recurring faults, root causes, and corrective actions.",
        "messages": [
          {
            "msg_id": "M59",
            "speaker_id": 386277,
            "reply_to": null,
            "text": "Hi team, I've completed the initial root cause analysis for the top 3 recurring faults as part of T6. The draft report A4 is in the project folder. The main causes appear to be sensor misalignment on the filler and belt tension drift on the main conveyor.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T6",
              "A4"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "magnifying_glass_tilted_left",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M60",
            "speaker_id": 95118,
            "reply_to": "M59",
            "text": "Thanks for this. The belt tension issue is definitely something we see a lot. It seems to get worse during longer runs, especially on night shift when they're running the heavier 'Super-C' product.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M61",
            "speaker_id": 11000,
            "reply_to": "M59",
            "text": "The tensioner assembly is old. We should just replace the whole thing. That would fix it for good!",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M62",
            "speaker_id": 33287,
            "reply_to": "M61",
            "text": "A full replacement is a major change and outside our project's scope. The RCA in A4 suggests the core issue is a lack of a standard calibration procedure. A more practical solution would be to develop a procedure and add a check to our new PM checklist.",
            "mentions": [
              11000
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A4"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M63",
            "speaker_id": 386277,
            "reply_to": "M62",
            "text": "I agree. For the sensor misalignment, the report A4 suggests we pilot some slightly adjusted machine settings. We could do this as part of T7. It's a low-cost action we can implement and test quickly.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A4",
              "T7"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M64",
            "speaker_id": 33287,
            "reply_to": "M63",
            "text": "Okay, so we have a few potential corrective actions. Given our limited time, we need to prioritize. I propose we focus on these two actions: 1) Develop a belt tension calibration SOP and add it to the PM. 2) Pilot the adjusted sensor settings (T7). This seems like the most impactful use of our time. D7",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T7"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D7"
            ],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "+1",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M65",
            "speaker_id": 95118,
            "reply_to": "M64",
            "text": "That sounds like a good plan. Those two issues cause the most downtime from what I see on the floor.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M66",
            "speaker_id": 11000,
            "reply_to": "M64",
            "text": "Ok, a new procedure is better than nothing. I can help write it.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M67",
            "speaker_id": 533175,
            "reply_to": "M64",
            "text": "The calibration procedure is the right approach. I saw a similar issue on Line 2 a few years ago and a standard procedure fixed it.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M68",
            "speaker_id": 33287,
            "reply_to": "M67",
            "text": "Consensus it is. D7 is confirmed. @386277, can you take the lead on documenting the calibration procedure and planning the pilot for T7?",
            "mentions": [
              386277
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T7"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D7"
            ],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "✅",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M69",
            "speaker_id": 386277,
            "reply_to": "M68",
            "text": "Yes, I can own that. I'll draft the procedure and coordinate with @95118 to schedule the T7 pilot run during a maintenance window next week.",
            "mentions": [
              95118
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T7"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M70",
            "speaker_id": 95118,
